Raise the hardcoded 3 second response timeout in the TUI scan dispatch path.

The TUI blocks on a synchronous recv_timeout while the engine builds the
snapshot, reads the entire address space of the target and runs the scan,
so on any process with a non-trivial RSS every scan reports a timeout and
ElementScannerPaneState::has_scan_results is never set. Because a subsequent
scan is gated on that flag, pressing 's' keeps issuing ScanNewRequest and
resets the snapshot instead of filtering the previous results.

Overridable at runtime via SQUALR_TUI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SECS.

Not upstream; the real fix is to keep the Receiver in the pane state and
poll it with try_recv from app_tick instead of blocking the key handler.
Bug: https://github.com/Squalr/Squalr/issues
--- a/squalr-tui/src/app/command_dispatch_scan.rs
+++ b/squalr-tui/src/app/command_dispatch_scan.rs
@@ -24,6 +24,19 @@
 use std::sync::mpsc;
 use std::time::{Duration, Instant};
 
+fn scan_command_response_timeout() -> Duration {
+    static SCAN_COMMAND_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT: std::sync::OnceLock<Duration> = std::sync::OnceLock::new();
+
+    *SCAN_COMMAND_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT.get_or_init(|| {
+        let timeout_in_seconds = std::env::var("SQUALR_TUI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SECS")
+            .ok()
+            .and_then(|timeout_in_seconds| timeout_in_seconds.parse::<u64>().ok())
+            .unwrap_or(120);
+
+        Duration::from_secs(timeout_in_seconds)
+    })
+}
